<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
</head>
<body>
<title>Barakah Books</title>
<meta name="claude:viewport-fit-sides" content="cover">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Amiri:wght@400;700&family=Bebas+Neue&family=Carlito:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&display=swap">
<style>
/* Layout: magenta hero (cover colour) with the real front cover beside the copy; then book-style navy section blocks, red-barred sub-titles, grey example boxes, green verse boxes and blue hadith boxes, as in the Handbook's own pages; closing band over the cash-register dials from the cover. */
:root{
  --bg:#FFFFFF; --band:#F4F0E6; --surface:#FFFFFF; --fg:#1C1C22; --muted:#555B66; --line:#D8D2C4;
  --navy:#1F4E79; --head:#1F4E79; --magenta:#A3305C; --red:#C0272D; --cream:#F1E3B3;
  --grey-box:#E7E5E1; --verse:#E2EFD9; --hadith:#DAE3F3;
  --btn-bg:#1F4E79; --btn-fg:#FFFFFF; --link:#1F4E79; --pattern:rgba(255,255,255,.1);
  --overlay:rgba(130,32,74,.88);
  --brass:#D9CBA0; --roller-a:#0B1626; --roller-b:#223A58;
  --font-display:'Bebas Neue','Arial Narrow',Impact,sans-serif;
  --font-body:'Carlito','Calibri',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;
  --font-ar:'Amiri','Noto Naskh Arabic',serif;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
    --bg:#0E141B; --band:#131C27; --surface:#172230; --fg:#E9E7E2; --muted:#A7ADB8; --line:#2C3847;
    --head:#8FB8E3; --red:#F0716D; --magenta:#7F2548; --grey-box:#1B2531; --verse:#17301F; --hadith:#17283F;
    --btn-bg:#3A7CC0; --btn-fg:#FFFFFF; --link:#8FB8E3; --pattern:rgba(255,255,255,.07);
    --overlay:rgba(70,16,40,.9); color-scheme:dark;
  }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{
  --bg:#0E141B; --band:#131C27; --surface:#172230; --fg:#E9E7E2; --muted:#A7ADB8; --line:#2C3847;
  --head:#8FB8E3; --red:#F0716D; --magenta:#7F2548; --grey-box:#1B2531; --verse:#17301F; --hadith:#17283F;
  --btn-bg:#3A7CC0; --btn-fg:#FFFFFF; --link:#8FB8E3; --pattern:rgba(255,255,255,.07);
  --overlay:rgba(70,16,40,.9); color-scheme:dark;
}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font-family:var(--font-body);font-size:17.5px;line-height:1.55}
h1,h2,h3{font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;line-height:1;margin:0;text-wrap:balance;text-transform:uppercase}
h4{margin:0}
p{margin:0}
a{color:var(--link)}
:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--link);outline-offset:3px}
.wrap{max-width:1120px;margin-inline:auto;padding-left:max(16px,env(safe-area-inset-left,0px));padding-right:max(16px,env(safe-area-inset-right,0px))}

/* Hero */
.hero{position:relative;background:var(--magenta);color:#FFFFFF;overflow:hidden}
.hero :focus-visible{outline-color:#FFFFFF}
.hero-pattern{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;pointer-events:none}
.hero .wrap{position:relative;padding-block:28px 72px}
.brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.7rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase}
.brand svg{width:26px;height:26px;flex:none;color:var(--cream)}
.hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr .85fr;gap:48px;align-items:center;margin-top:40px}
.hero-grid>*{min-width:0}
.bismillah{font-family:var(--font-ar);font-size:2.1rem;color:var(--cream);margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.4}
.hero h1{font-size:clamp(3.4rem,9vw,6.6rem);line-height:.92;color:#FFFFFF}
.hero .lede{font-size:1.25rem;max-width:34rem;margin-top:22px}
.price-label{margin-top:28px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.15rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--cream)}
.register{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin-top:8px;font-family:var(--font-display)}
.register .d,.register .cur{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:2.4rem;height:3.5rem;border-radius:4px;font-size:2.7rem;line-height:1;color:#F1E6C4;background:linear-gradient(var(--roller-a),var(--roller-b) 50%,var(--roller-a));box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px var(--brass),0 3px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.3)}
.register .dot{font-size:2.7rem;line-height:1;margin-inline:-2px}
.register .aud{font-size:1.4rem;letter-spacing:.1em;margin-left:8px}
.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin-top:30px}
.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:50px;padding:0 26px;border-radius:4px;font:700 1.05rem var(--font-body);letter-spacing:.02em;text-decoration:none;cursor:pointer;border:2px solid transparent}
.btn-white{background:#FFFFFF;color:#7A1F46}
.btn-white:hover{background:var(--cream)}
.btn-line{border-color:#FFFFFF;color:#FFFFFF;background:transparent}
.btn-line:hover{background:rgba(255,255,255,.14)}
.btn-main{background:var(--btn-bg);color:var(--btn-fg);width:100%}
.btn-main:hover{filter:brightness(1.1)}
.cover-fig{margin:0}
.cover-fig img{display:block;width:100%;max-width:380px;height:auto;margin-inline:auto;box-shadow:0 28px 44px rgba(0,0,0,.4),0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.3);transform:rotate(-2.5deg)}
.cover-fig figcaption{font-size:.9rem;text-align:center;margin-top:18px;color:#FFFFFF;opacity:.92}

/* Section titles in the Handbook's style */
section{padding-block:76px}
.sec-head{display:block;max-width:600px;background:var(--navy);color:#FFFFFF;font-size:clamp(2.8rem,7vw,4.4rem);text-align:right;padding:22px 26px 14px;letter-spacing:.01em}
.bar-title{display:block;max-width:44rem;margin-top:28px;padding:8px 18px;border-inline:6px solid var(--red);color:var(--head);text-align:center;font-size:clamp(2rem,4.6vw,3rem);line-height:1.02}
.sec-lede{max-width:42rem;margin-top:18px;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.15rem}
.rtitle{color:var(--red);font:700 .86rem var(--font-body);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;padding-bottom:5px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--red)}
.rtitle .ref{margin-left:10px;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:.06em;white-space:nowrap}

/* Inside the book */
.inside-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:56px;margin-top:36px;align-items:start}
.inside-grid>*{min-width:0}
.inside-text p+p{margin-top:14px}
.facts{margin:24px 0 0;padding:0;list-style:none;border-top:1px solid var(--red)}
.facts li{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.facts li span:first-child{font-weight:700;color:var(--red);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;font-size:.84rem;padding-top:3px}
.facts li span:last-child{text-align:right;min-width:0}
.toc{margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none}
.toc li{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:6px;padding:7px 0}
.toc .t{min-width:0}
.toc .lead{flex:1;min-width:16px;border-bottom:2px dotted var(--muted);transform:translateY(-4px)}
.toc .p{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}

/* Offer */
.offer{background:var(--band);border-block:1px solid var(--line)}
.offer-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:48px;margin-top:36px;align-items:start}
.offer-grid>*{min-width:0}
.spec{margin:0;border-top:1px solid var(--red)}
.spec div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:9.5rem 1fr;gap:16px;padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.spec dt{font-weight:700;color:var(--red);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;font-size:.84rem;padding-top:3px}
.spec dd{margin:0;min-width:0}
.order{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:26px}
.order h3{font-size:2.2rem;color:var(--head)}
.order .note{color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px}
.lab,.order legend{display:block;margin-bottom:8px;padding:0;color:var(--red);font:700 .84rem var(--font-body);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase}
.field{margin-top:22px}
fieldset.field{border:0;padding:0;margin:22px 0 0;min-width:0}
.qty-row{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px}
.qty-row .lab{margin:0}
.stepper{display:flex;align-items:center}
.stepper button{width:44px;height:44px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:700 1.3rem var(--font-body);cursor:pointer}
.stepper button:first-child{border-radius:4px 0 0 4px}
.stepper button:last-child{border-radius:0 4px 4px 0}
.stepper input{width:64px;height:44px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-inline:0;background:var(--surface);color:var(--fg);text-align:center;font:700 1.15rem var(--font-body);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;border-radius:0;-moz-appearance:textfield}
.stepper input::-webkit-outer-spin-button,.stepper input::-webkit-inner-spin-button{-webkit-appearance:none;margin:0}
.plan{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:12px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;background:var(--bg);cursor:pointer}
.plan+.plan{margin-top:8px}
.plan input{margin-top:5px;accent-color:var(--navy)}
.plan:has(input:checked){border-color:var(--link);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--link)}
.plan b{display:block}
.plan span span{color:var(--muted);font-size:.98rem}
select{width:100%;height:46px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:400 1.05rem var(--font-body);padding:0 10px}
.lines{margin:22px 0 0;padding:0;list-style:none;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.lines li{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.lines li span:first-child{min-width:0}
.lines li.total{font-weight:700;font-size:1.25rem}
.lines li.sub{color:var(--muted);font-size:1rem}
.offer-text{margin-top:20px;padding:14px;border-radius:4px;background:var(--grey-box);font-size:1rem}
.offer-text b{font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:1.4rem;letter-spacing:.03em;text-transform:uppercase;display:block;margin-bottom:4px;color:var(--head)}
.agree{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;margin-top:16px}
.agree input{margin-top:6px;accent-color:var(--navy);flex:none}
.order .btn{margin-top:18px}
.fine{font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:12px}
.receipt{margin-top:18px;padding:16px;border:2px solid var(--link);border-radius:4px}
.receipt strong{display:block;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:1.6rem;letter-spacing:.03em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--head)}
.receipt ul{margin:0;padding-left:1.1rem}
.receipt li+li{margin-top:6px}

/* Rulings */
.rules-wrap{margin-top:44px}
.rules-group{display:grid;grid-template-columns:15rem 1fr;gap:16px 44px;padding-block:34px;border-top:3px solid var(--navy)}
.rules-group:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.rules-group>*{min-width:0}
.rules-group .gh{align-self:start}
.rules-group .bar-title{margin-top:0;font-size:2.1rem;padding:6px 12px;border-inline-width:5px}
.rules-group .pp{margin-top:10px;text-align:center;font-size:.86rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}
.rule+.rule{margin-top:26px}
.rule p{margin-top:8px}
.ex,.hadith,.verse{margin-top:10px;padding:10px 12px;font-size:.98rem;border-block:1px solid var(--line)}
.ex{background:var(--grey-box)}
.hadith{background:var(--hadith);font-style:italic}
.verse{background:var(--verse);font-style:italic}
.ex b{font-style:normal}

/* Closing */
.closing{background:linear-gradient(var(--overlay),var(--overlay)),url("data:image/jpeg;base64,") center 40%/cover no-repeat;color:#FFFFFF;padding-block:84px}
.closing blockquote{margin:0;max-width:46rem}
.closing blockquote p{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5.6vw,3.8rem);line-height:1.02;text-transform:uppercase;text-wrap:balance}
.closing cite{display:block;margin-top:20px;font-style:normal;color:var(--cream);font-weight:700}
footer{padding-block:30px;font-size:.95rem;color:var(--muted)}
footer p+p{margin-top:8px}

@media (max-width:880px){
  .hero-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:36px;margin-top:30px}
  .cover-fig img{max-width:320px}
  .inside-grid,.offer-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:36px}
  .rules-group{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .rules-group .gh{max-width:22rem}
  section{padding-block:54px}
}
@media (max-width:520px){
  .spec div{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2px}
  .hero .wrap{padding-bottom:48px}
  .register .d,.register .cur{width:2rem;height:3rem;font-size:2.3rem}
  .sec-head{padding:18px 18px 10px}
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){
  .btn{transition:background .15s,filter .15s}
}
</style>

<svg width="0" height="0" style="position:absolute" aria-hidden="true">
  <symbol id="star" viewBox="0 0 40 40"><polygon points="8,8 32,8 32,32 8,32" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><polygon points="20,1.7 38.3,20 20,38.3 1.7,20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></symbol>
</svg>

<header class="hero">
  <svg class="hero-pattern" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <defs>
      <pattern id="tile" width="80" height="80" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
        <polygon points="20,20 60,20 60,60 20,60" fill="none" stroke="var(--pattern)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        <polygon points="40,11.7 68.3,40 40,68.3 11.7,40" fill="none" stroke="var(--pattern)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        <circle cx="40" cy="40" r="11" fill="none" stroke="var(--pattern)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
      </pattern>
    </defs>
    <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#tile)"/>
  </svg>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="brand"><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#star"/></svg>Barakah Books</div>
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="bismillah" lang="ar" dir="rtl" style="text-align:left">بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم</div>
        <h1>Know your trade before you trade.</h1>
        <p class="lede">The Money Handbook is a concise textbook about wealth and financial dealings in Islam, by Mufti Aasim Rashid. We sell it the way it teaches: clear goods, a clear price and clear terms, all written down before you say yes.</p>
        <p class="price-label">Fixed price, per copy</p>
        <div class="register" role="img" aria-label="Price: 15 dollars and 00 cents, Australian dollars">
          <span class="cur" aria-hidden="true">$</span><span class="d" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="d" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">.</span><span class="d" aria-hidden="true">0</span><span class="d" aria-hidden="true">0</span><span class="aud" aria-hidden="true">AUD</span>
        </div>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-white" href="#offer">See the full offer</a>
          <a class="btn btn-line" href="#rulings">See the rulings this sale follows</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="cover-fig">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="900" height="1311" alt="Front cover of The Money Handbook by Mufti Aasim Rashid: a red cash register with number dials, a magenta author panel, and the subtitle A concise textbook about wealth and financial dealings in Islam.">
        <figcaption>The front cover of the printed Handbook.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <section id="inside">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="sec-head">Inside the book</h2>
      <h3 class="bar-title">Thirteen topics on earning and spending the halal way</h3>
      <p class="sec-lede">Written as a course textbook. Verses and hadith are referenced, examples use everyday English, and short discussion questions help you apply each idea.</p>

      <div class="inside-grid">
        <div class="inside-text">
          <p>The Handbook opens with how the Qur’an describes wealth, then moves to the rules of buying and selling: what can be sold, how a price must be set, how a deal is agreed, and the options a buyer or seller can keep.</p>
          <p>It closes with ethics, rent, work and wages, and the two money questions most people face today: interest and credit cards. It sticks to matters of general agreement in mainstream fiqh.</p>
          <ul class="facts">
            <li><span>Author</span><span>Mufti Aasim Rashid</span></li>
            <li><span>Text completed</span><span>July 2018</span></li>
            <li><span>Length</span><span>About 40 pages</span></li>
            <li><span>Best for</span><span>Students and anyone who earns or spends</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <ol class="toc">
          <li><span class="t">Wealth in the Qur’an</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">6</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Trade and sales</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">11</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Components and requisites of a sale</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">12</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">The transaction: offer and acceptance</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">17</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Types of sales</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">18</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Options</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">21</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Transaction outcomes</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">24</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Ethics</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">26</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Rent and lease</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">27</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Hiring and employment</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">28</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Interest</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">31</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Bank accounts</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">36</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">Credit cards</span><span class="lead"></span><span class="p">37</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="offer" id="offer">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="sec-head">The offer</h2>
      <h3 class="bar-title">Everything you agree to is written here first</h3>
      <p class="sec-lede">Our offer is stated in full below. You accept it by saying so clearly, and the acceptance matches the offer exactly.</p>

      <div class="offer-grid">
        <dl class="spec">
          <div><dt>Item</dt><dd>The Money Handbook: A concise textbook about wealth and financial dealings in Islam, by Mufti Aasim Rashid</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Type and condition</dt><dd>Printed copy, A4, about 40 pages. New and unused, with no known defects.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Your copy</dt><dd>30 copies are on our shelf. Your copy is set aside and numbered when you accept.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Price</dt><dd>$15.00 AUD per copy when you pay in full. Or $16.50 AUD per copy in 3 instalments of $5.50. You choose before you accept.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Postage</dt><dd>$5.00 AUD per order, shown in your total.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Payment</dt><dd>Money, in Australian dollars. Pay by debit card, pre-paid card or bank transfer, chosen before you accept. We ask for the first payment before we post.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Delivery</dt><dd>Posted within 2 business days of your first payment. It reaches you no later than 7 days after you accept, and the exact date is shown before you accept.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Return option</dt><dd>7 days from the day you receive the copy, for any reason. Tell us before you send it back.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Defects and wrong descriptions</dt><dd>Full refund, no deductions, and we agree to it now.</dd></div>
        </dl>

        <form class="order" id="order" aria-labelledby="order-h">
          <h3 id="order-h">Your order</h3>
          <p class="note">Change anything you like. Nothing is agreed until you press the last button.</p>

          <div class="field">
            <div class="qty-row">
              <label class="lab" for="qty">Copies</label>
              <div class="stepper">
                <button type="button" id="minus" aria-label="One fewer copy">−</button>
                <input id="qty" type="number" min="1" max="5" value="1" inputmode="numeric">
                <button type="button" id="plus" aria-label="One more copy">+</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <fieldset class="field">
            <legend>How you pay</legend>
            <label class="plan"><input type="radio" name="plan" value="full" checked><span><b>Pay in full now</b><span>$15.00 per copy</span></span></label>
            <label class="plan"><input type="radio" name="plan" value="inst"><span><b>Pay in 3 instalments</b><span>$5.50 per copy each time, $16.50 in all. The price is fixed once you choose.</span></span></label>
          </fieldset>

          <div class="field">
            <label class="lab" for="method">Payment method</label>
            <select id="method">
              <option value="debit card">Debit card</option>
              <option value="pre-paid card">Pre-paid card</option>
              <option value="bank transfer">Bank transfer</option>
            </select>
          </div>

          <ul class="lines" id="lines" aria-live="polite"></ul>

          <div class="offer-text" id="offer-text" aria-live="polite"></div>

          <label class="agree" for="adult"><input type="checkbox" id="adult" required><span>I am 18 or over, or my parent or guardian agrees to this purchase.</span></label>

          <button class="btn btn-main" type="submit">I buy it on these terms</button>
          <p class="fine">“I’m interested” does not complete a sale, so the button above is the clear acceptance. If you leave this page the offer ends. Accept again when you return.</p>
          <div class="receipt" id="receipt" hidden aria-live="polite"></div>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="rulings">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="sec-head">The rulings</h2>
      <h3 class="bar-title">Every term of this sale comes from the Handbook</h3>
      <p class="sec-lede">Each rule below names its Handbook page, states what the book teaches, and then shows how this sale follows it.</p>

      <div class="rules-wrap">

        <div class="rules-group">
          <div class="gh"><h3 class="bar-title">The merchandise</h3><p class="pp">Handbook pp. 12–13</p></div>
          <div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">It exists, is owned and is in hand<span class="ref">p. 12</span></h4><p>The item must exist at the time of sale, belong to a specific owner, and be deliverable. The seller must have it in his possession.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> Every copy is printed, owned by us and on our shelf. We take no pre-orders.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">A specific copy<span class="ref">p. 12</span></h4><p>The good being sold must be designated. A deal to sell “one of a dozen watches” is not valid.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> Your copy is numbered and set aside when you accept.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Quantity and quality are clear<span class="ref">p. 12</span></h4><p>The buyer must be clear on the quantity, type and quality. A misleading description makes the sale invalid.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> The offer states the type, size, page count and condition: new, A4, about 40 pages.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">A lawful good<span class="ref">p. 13</span></h4><p>The merchandise must be a lawful good or commodity.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> A textbook on lawful earning and spending. It is nowhere near the Handbook’s list of unlawful commodities.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rules-group">
          <div class="gh"><h3 class="bar-title">Price and payment</h3><p class="pp">Handbook pp. 13–14</p></div>
          <div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">The exact amount<span class="ref">p. 13</span></h4><p>The full amount must be clear at the time of sale. Hidden costs cannot be added after the buyer agrees, and a buyer cannot purchase for an undisclosed amount.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> $15.00 per copy plus $5.00 postage. Your total shows before you accept.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Form, currency and mode<span class="ref">p. 14</span></h4><p>The form of payment (money, goods or services), the currency, and the mode (cash, card or transfer) must be settled before the sale is complete.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> Money in Australian dollars, by debit card, pre-paid card or bank transfer. The Handbook calls debit and pre-paid cards better alternatives to regular credit cards (p. 38).</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Date and schedule<span class="ref">p. 14</span></h4><p>The date and schedule of payment must be set during the transaction. A deal where “later” is left unclear is not permitted.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> You pay when you accept, or on three dates shown in the offer.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Who pays first<span class="ref">p. 14</span></h4><p>When the payment is money, the seller has the right to ask for it before handing over the item.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> We ask for your first payment before we post your copy.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rules-group">
          <div class="gh"><h3 class="bar-title">The agreement</h3><p class="pp">Handbook pp. 15–17</p></div>
          <div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">The parties<span class="ref">p. 15</span></h4><p>Buyer and seller must be sane and old enough to understand the deal. A child who can discern may buy goods with a guardian’s permission.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> If you are under 18, a parent or guardian must agree. The order form asks you to confirm.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Offer and acceptance<span class="ref">p. 17</span></h4><p>A sale needs an offer and an acceptance, in words that leave no doubt. “I’m interested” does not finish a deal, and the acceptance must match the offer. If either party walks away before accepting, the offer is void.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> Our offer is written in full. You accept with “I buy it on these terms”. If you leave the page, the offer ends.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Possession and risk<span class="ref">pp. 15–16</span></h4><p>Whoever has possession carries the risk of the item. Possession passes to the buyer when the item is handed over or is in his control.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> Until your copy is in your hands, any loss or damage is ours. We replace it or refund you in full.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rules-group">
          <div class="gh"><h3 class="bar-title">Credit and interest</h3><p class="pp">Handbook pp. 19, 33</p></div>
          <div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Instalments on set terms<span class="ref">p. 19</span></h4><p>Buying in instalments is permitted if the final amount is fixed, the payment schedule is set, no penalty is charged for a late payment, and the price does not rise if the buyer asks for more time. A seller may offer separate cash and credit prices.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> $15.00 cash, or 3 × $5.50 ($16.50). The dates appear in the offer before you accept.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">No penalty, no interest<span class="ref">pp. 19, 33</span></h4><p>A penalty for a delayed or missed payment is interest, and taking it is unlawful.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> No late fees, no interest and no price rise for more time.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rules-group">
          <div class="gh"><h3 class="bar-title">Your options</h3><p class="pp">Handbook pp. 21–23</p></div>
          <div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Return option<span class="ref">p. 21</span></h4><p>A party may keep the right to withdraw within a set time. It must be placed before the deal is complete, with a time limit, and the other party must witness it. The holder must give notice. It ends when the time is up, when the buyer uses the item, or when the holder says the sale is final. If the item is damaged within the period, the buyer replaces it or pays its full value.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> 7 days from the day you receive your copy. It is written here before you accept and your receipt repeats it. Tell us before you send it back.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Description option<span class="ref">p. 21</span></h4><p>If an item is sold with a claimed feature and the feature turns out to be false, the sale can be cancelled.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> If a chapter or pages this page promised are missing, you may cancel for a full refund.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Price option<span class="ref">pp. 21–22</span></h4><p>A merchant may sell above or below market value if the customer agrees, but may not trick the customer into thinking it is market value. A tricked customer may return the item for full repayment, if he has not used it since learning of the fraud.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> We make no claim about market value and show no invented “was” price. $15.00 is simply our price.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Inspection option<span class="ref">p. 22</span></h4><p>A buyer who buys without seeing the item may see it before deciding. Once he has seen it to the usual extent, he must decide.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> You buy without holding the book, so when it arrives you may look it over, then keep it or return it.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Defect option<span class="ref">pp. 22–23</span></h4><p>A seller must disclose any defect. If a defect existed at the time of sale and was not disclosed, the buyer may keep the item at the agreed price or return it, and the seller may not keep part of the price. After the buyer takes possession, the seller’s consent or a court decision is needed.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> We know of no defects. If one existed when we sold it, we agree now to take the copy back and refund you in full, with no deductions.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rules-group">
          <div class="gh"><h3 class="bar-title">No strings attached</h3><p class="pp">Handbook p. 24</p></div>
          <div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">No defective conditions<span class="ref">p. 24</span></h4><p>A sale is defective if the seller bars the buyer from using the item for a period, from selling it on, or from inspecting it. It is also defective if the item, price or dates are left vague, such as “whatever it is worth” or “as soon as possible”.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> We attach none of these conditions. You may use, lend, give or resell your copy. Using it only ends the 7-day return option.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rules-group">
          <div class="gh"><h3 class="bar-title">Manners of trade</h3><p class="pp">Handbook pp. 25–26</p></div>
          <div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Truthful, complete disclosure<span class="ref">p. 26</span></h4><p>The seller must give full and truthful information about the product, including its type, origin and cost.</p><p class="hadith">Trade is blessed when both sides speak truthfully and disclose fully, and the blessing is erased by lies and hiding details. (Bukhari 2079, 2082)</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> Everything about the book and its price is stated above.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Ease of conduct<span class="ref">p. 26</span></h4><p>Buyer and seller should not be harsh in their terms or insist on prices that are too high or too low.</p><p class="hadith">May Allah have mercy on one who is lenient when he sells, buys and collects payment. (Bukhari)</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> Every buyer pays the same price on gentle terms.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">No hoarding<span class="ref">p. 26</span></h4><p>A merchant must not hold essential goods back until supply runs out and then sell at an exorbitant price.</p><p class="hadith">One who hoards is sinful. (Muslim 1605)</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> We never hold copies back to raise the price.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Avoiding oaths<span class="ref">p. 26</span></h4><p>Even a truthful oath should not be used to sell merchandise.</p><p class="hadith">Swearing may help sell goods, but it erases the blessing. (Bukhari 2087)</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> Plain sales talk, with no swearing.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">No cutting in, no fake bids<span class="ref">p. 25</span></h4><p>While two parties are making a deal, a third party may not cut in with his own offer, and raising a bid without meaning to buy is also forbidden.</p><p class="hadith">Do not interrupt your brother’s trade with your own trade. Do not raise bids without intending to buy. (Muslim)</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> We never push into another seller’s deal and never fake praise. We have no customer reviews yet, so none are shown.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Frequent charity<span class="ref">p. 26</span></h4><p>A merchant should pay charity often, to make up for any swearing, dishonesty or poor conduct in trade.</p><p class="hadith">Oaths and lies appear in business, so mix your trade with charity. (Tirmidhi 1208)</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> We give $1 of every copy sold to charity.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">A written record<span class="ref">p. 26</span></h4><p>It is desirable that all contracts and loans are written down and witnessed, and that all delayed sales and debts are documented.</p><p class="verse">Qur’an 2:282 prescribes writing down debts and delayed payments.</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> Your receipt lists every term, and the instalment dates if you choose that plan.</p></div>
            <div class="rule"><h4 class="rtitle">Jumu‘ah comes first<span class="ref">p. 25</span></h4><p>Buying or selling after the adhan of Jumu‘ah is makruh. The sale may stand, but the person is sinful for breaking the command.</p><p class="verse">When the call to prayer is given on Friday, hurry to the remembrance of Allah and leave trade. (Qur’an 62:9)</p><p class="ex"><b>This sale:</b> Our orders and postage pause during the Friday prayer.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="closing">
    <div class="wrap">
      <blockquote>
        <p>The honest and trustworthy merchant will be raised with the prophets, the true followers and the martyrs.</p>
        <cite>Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, Jami‘ al-Tirmidhi 1209, as quoted in The Money Handbook, p. 5</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

